---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SizeReader from '../components/SizeReader.astro';
import WorkOrder from '../components/WorkOrder.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Tires | Oakspur Tire & Wheel, Kansas City"
  description="All-season, truck, winter and used tires in Kansas City, installed the same day. Every price includes mounting, balancing, valve stems and disposal."
>
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <h1>Tires for how you drive</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      We keep the common sizes on the rack and can get most others by the next morning. Tell us what
      you drive and what you want to spend, and we'll show you two or three that fit.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <ul class="kinds">
        <li>
          <h2>All-season</h2>
          <p>
            The right tire for most Kansas City cars and crossovers. Quiet on the highway, steady in
            rain, fine in a light snow.
          </p>
          <p class="kinds__fits">Good for commuters and family cars.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h2>Truck and SUV</h2>
          <p>
            Highway, all-terrain and load-rated tires for pickups and SUVs. Tell us if you tow or
            haul and we'll match the load rating.
          </p>
          <p class="kinds__fits">Good for work trucks, trailers and gravel roads.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h2>Winter</h2>
          <p>
            Softer rubber that grips below 45 degrees. We'll mount a set on spare wheels so the
            spring and fall swap takes 20 minutes.
          </p>
          <p class="kinds__fits">Good for hills, early shifts and rear-wheel drive.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h2>Used</h2>
          <p>
            Inspected inside and out, with at least half their tread left. The tread depth and the
            price are written on every one in yellow crayon.
          </p>
          <p class="kinds__fits">Good for a tight budget or matching one damaged tire.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--paper">
    <div class="wrap split split--wide-right">
      <div>
        <h2>Start with your size</h2>
        <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1rem">
          It's printed on the sidewall of the tires you have now and on the sticker inside your
          driver's door.
        </p>
        <p>
          The wrong size can rub, throw off your speedometer or fail to carry the weight of your
          vehicle. If you're thinking about a different size, call us first.
        </p>
      </div>
      <SizeReader />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>What a set of four costs</h2>
        <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1rem">
          Here's an example for a common crossover size. Your price depends on the tire
          you pick, but the list of what's included never changes.
        </p>
        <ul class="ruled">
          <li>
            <h3>Payment</h3>
            <p>Cash, debit and all major cards. Ask at the counter about paying over six months.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Warranty</h3>
            <p>
              New tires carry the maker's tread warranty. We handle the paperwork if you ever need
              to use it.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <WorkOrder />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .kinds {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
  }

  .kinds li {
    padding-block: 1.75rem;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--rubber);
  }

  .kinds h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.6vw, 2rem);
  }

  .kinds p {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .kinds__fits {
    margin-bottom: 0 !important;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--oak);
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .kinds {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      column-gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
    }
  }
</style>
